                    text: "Module factories already run at 35–40% of capacity, and cell capacity is forecast to go from about 35 GW to about 60 GW by March 2027 (CRISIL) and 100 GW by December 2027 (ICRA), against FY27 demand of 60–65 GW. When that arrives, the premium that earns **Emmvee** ₹8.5–9 a watt and **Websol** its 34% margin will narrow, and the module makers opening cell lines (**Vikram**, **Saatvik**, **Insolation**, **Alpex**, **Solex**) will get a smaller prize than they planned for. Chinese cell prices fell again in September (EnergyTrend), widening the gap buyers pay for Indian cells and keeping pressure on the rule. **Most managements acknowledged falling prices but not how far they could go.**",
